Build, lead and grow a high\-performing team of data engineers, including hiring and talent development, balancing hands\-on technical involvement with people leadership as the team scales, and fostering a culture of ownership, business orientation, quality, and continuous improvement;
Own the IT delivery of data engineering initiatives across a complex, large\-scale landscape, collaborating with multiple teams and stakeholder groups to ensure reliable outcomes in a demanding and fast\-paced business environment;
Partner with other engineering disciplines (software, integration and AI) as well as architecture to contribute to devising the technical direction for the data platform / data engineering products and ensure synergies are exploited across the various teams;
Drive the adoption of AI within data engineering, from AI\-assisted development and tooling to embedding AI\-driven capabilities into data pipelines and platforms;
Ensure operational excellence across the data platform, keeping it reliable, cost\-effective, and performant while continuously working to minimize operational efforts and overhead;
Collaborate with the relevant IT and platform management organizations to drive the implementation of data quality, observability, and governance topics within the data platform.

Track record delivering large\-scale, complex products in demanding environments with significant technical and organizational complexity;
Proven experience (5\+ years) leading engineering teams, including people leadership, hiring, coaching, and performance development;
Proven experience operating platforms in production at scale, including monitoring, incident management, and driving reliability and operational efficiency over time;Strong hands\-on expertise across hybrid architectures, both transactional/operational systems and analytical platforms (data warehouses, lakes), and how to integrate them;
Knowledge and experience with Azure, Snowflake, dbt and are of advantage;
Solid engineering fundamentals spanning both classical core software engineering practices (e.g., testing, architecture patterns, CI/CD) and modern data engineering (e.g., pipeline design, data modeling, cloud data platforms, data observability);
Ability to operate at different levels: technically strong to make hands\-on contributions and credible technical calls, while equally committed to the people side of the role developing a high performing team;
Good understanding of how AI is changing engineering practices, from AI\-assisted development and testing to its implications for data platforms and team ways of working;
Strong stakeholder management, able to work with architecture, product, and business functions and translate between them;
Communicates with confidence and clarity, distilling technical and delivery trade\-offs into language that lands with engineers and business stakeholders alike;
Experience in financial services and/or asset management is an advantage.
Excellent English oral and written communication skills; German is a plus.
